module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.tco_identity_passthrough_elision_after_slot_local_split

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data tco_identity_passthrough_elision_after_slot_local_split: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "tco_identity_passthrough_elision_after_slot_local_split" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**CLASS: an optimization that treats source-level name equality as state identity after lowering has split one source binding into a mutable local and a persistent state slot; it elides a required transfer and turns a terminating tail-recursive loop into a fixed-point loop.** INVALID STATE: TCO loop parameters `__tco_loop_*` with authored names rebound each iteration from those slots; a tail self-call whose argument is the same-named ExprVar as a parameter emits `continue` with no slot write because identity-passthrough treated spelling equality as a no-op assign.",

    "CORRECTION: tail-call lowering assigns every state slot from the fully evaluated argument vector; source spelling equality never licenses omission after the slot/local split. Production `emit_typed_tco_reassign` / `emit_typed_tco_reassign_shared` both reach `shared_tco_reassign` → `tco_reassign_core` with every parameter. There is no production identity filter and no authored mutant of that filter: a copy that omits dests by construction cannot red production.",

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN (2026-09-15, gunbc#11422, parent fierce-seal-607). After `bcf770451ee` rebinding authored names as `let mut tokens = __tco_loop_tokens.clone()`, `parse_arg_list_acc` / `parse_param_list_acc` still emitted a bare `continue` on the 2+ item list arm. Required CI printed nothing after `phase floor ROUTED` and was cancelled at the 90/180 minute caps.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS versus `tco_rewrite_binds_named_arguments_positionally`: that class writes every slot but binds named tail-call arguments by POSITION, so a permuted label lands in the wrong parameter. This class writes NO slot when the argument spelling matches the parameter. THE DISCRIMINATOR is production emit of a same-named reassigned tail arg: restore identity-passthrough and the Rust #[test] `tco_tail_call_assigns_every_loop_slot` fails dest count on the walk fixture. That test is off the required floor (`rust_unit_tests_off_the_merge_path`). An authored copy of the deleted filter cannot red production.",

    "CONTROLS, AT THEIR ACTUAL STANDING. The ENROLLED wall is the required build lane: it compiles the regenerated seed and runs it over the corpus, so a hang from this class is caught as a timeout (rung 1, mitigatable; it fired on gunbc#11422). No required floor witness can import v1.compiler.emit — witnesses.yml source roots are dag + src/v2 only, and adding v1 is a job-roster change. Emitter-grain local diligence is `v1.tests.claim.tco_tail_call_assigns_every_loop_slot_witness` `tco_shared_reassign_writes_every_slot_in_param_order` (shared_tco_reassign dests; compile_dag_rust_emit_check is not used here because the seed has no v1_rt realization of that builtin). The Rust #[test]s `tco_tail_call_assigns_every_loop_slot` and `parse_multiline_two_param_fn_and_two_arg_call_yields_expected_module` are the same standing (`rust_unit_tests_off_the_merge_path`).",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable — a hang on the required build lane, caught as a timeout. CEILING: structurally guaranteed once every TCO reassign writes every slot from its argument expression. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a CI lane that executes v1.compiler witnesses (the capability; today it is a declared gap, not a witness that can be added under dag + src/v2).",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
